						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, December 30, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Sacred Honor Disbanding </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Sacred Honor Guild will be disbanding as of the end of 2004. We regret that the guildname will no longer be seen around Norrath on Solusek Ro but feel retiring the good name of Sacred Honor preferential to handing it off to another like a hand-me-down article of clothing. Sacred Honor maintained a good reputation with the majority of Norrath and succeeded in accomplishing a great many things, not only for it's members but also for allies, friends and relative strangers within the realm of Norrath. <BR>Caio!<BR>Selias Trailtracker<BR>(guildleader of Sacred Honor)
							<br><BR>
							 - Selias Trailtracker<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=592">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><BR><img src=images/redline.gif height=2 width="100%"><BR><BR></TD></TR>
					

						<TR><TD><p class="pTitle">The Time Has Come... </p></TD></TR>
							<TR><TD><p class=pText>
							As Selias has already stated, SH will become a Myth in the winds of Norrath.  However, we have moved on to WoW, Whisperwind Server in the form of the "Mythfits".<BR><BR>Over the past 3 years we have watched several young ones grow up, spread their wings and move on to Raiding Guilds such as DB, Triadica, Empy and others.  Unlike other Guilds that have handed the reins to another, we decided to just disband SH and let our people move forth to new aspirations and lands.  We will pop up from time to time, so don't think you have gotten rid or Sunny & Ecc or Selias & Adra.<BR><BR>We will miss many and will hope to cross paths again in the future of the gaming world.  Always feel welcome to come say Hi and watch the metamorphis of changes to the SH Site over the next several days!<BR><BR>Adrastea - Sacred Honor Retired Guild Liaison<BR>Adra - Mythfits - Head Mythtress
							 <BR><BR>- Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=593">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp; <a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=593">[View Comments]</a>

					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, December 17, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Mystic Crusaders Looking for New Recruits. </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Mystic Crusaders are looking for a few good adventures to fill the slots of those that have journeyed on to WoW and EQ2.  If you are looking for a wild bunch of peeps with a great sense of humor and a willingness to go just about anywheres on norrath you should make it a point to check us out.  http://www.mysticcrusaders.org/main.htm<BR>Check us out or find one of us in game we'd be more than glad to help ya out.  -Anjilkins
							<br><BR>
							 - Aengel<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=591">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Wednesday, December 15, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Lords of Prophecy </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							"Lords of Prophecy" is looking for motivated and fun people who play during US evening times. We are L65+ raiding family with "no-drama" policy. <BR><BR>Visit us at www.VYTCO.com or tell in game to Krushor, Berrywine or Flaor for more info.
							<br><BR>
							 - Flaor McLife<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=589">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><BR><img src=images/redline.gif height=2 width="100%"><BR><BR></TD></TR>
					

						<TR><TD><p class="pTitle">Grats to Eye of Mordor/Corona Mundi! </p></TD></TR>
							<TR><TD><p class=pText>
							The CMEOM Alliance took down Solusek Ro last night to become, finally, fully Elemental. To Time! Rar!
							 <BR><BR>- Sodoshi<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=588">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Friday, December 03, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Death Misdealt is now Recruiting </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Death Misdealt is now actively recruiting all classes level 55 and above for fun and adventure.  If you would like to join us visit our web site and drop us a message on the forums.<BR><BR>Aaethdor <BR>Guildleader Death Misdealt
							<br><BR>
							 - Aaethdor<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=587">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Saturday, November 20, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">CHANGE IN PLANS ! </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Cause of our similar raid goals and wishes to pwn  many raid challenges per-night , Veterans of Solusek is now drafting 65+s into Echoes of Honor lead by Nurmall , VoS will remain a guild to continue letting lower lvls in, and then have them drafted into EoH ! Soo if any persons wish to join us in a fight for flags/xp/loot and Xtra PWNAGE SAUCE , plz contact Biko for VoS or get in touch with me for 65+ recruitment for EoH !
							<br><BR>
							 - Biko<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=585">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=585">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Saturday, November 13, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Knights of Nobility Inviting New Members </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Hail, Good Citizens of Norrath!<BR><BR>The Grand Duke and Grand Duchess of the Knights of Nobility cordially invite you to visit our earthly Fortress. Here, you can find out more about our organization, and determine if you are worthy of our ranks! At this time, we are reducing our level requirements to the 25th season in order to allow more opportunity for newcomers to enjoy what we have to offer.<BR><BR>Please click on the Guilds link on the left, then find Knights of Nobility in the list, and you will be directed to our Fortress. If you find that you have an interest in joining, please fill out our application and locate a Knight in Norrath.
							<br><BR>
							 - Tuwini<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=584">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Thursday, November 11, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">New Members </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							Novus Satus is currently seeking new members. Please vist us at www.novussatus.com<BR><BR>Thanks<BR>Genalebe Layurhands<BR>Guild Leader of Novus Satus
							<br><BR>
							 - Genalebe<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=583">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							<BR><BR></TD></TR>
					
						<tr><td bgcolor=FFCC00><p class="pDate">Monday, November 08, 2004</p></TD></TR>
						<tr><td><BR><p class="pTitle">Legion of the White Rose - Passing of the Torch </p>
							<tr><td><p class=pText>
							I'd like to formally announce and acknowledge Lady Gentlewind as the new Guildmistress of the Legacy chapter of the Legion of the White Rose.  Lady Gentlewind has been a Legionnaire for over 2 years and has earned the respect and admiration of her Guildmates.  <BR><BR>This change comes in preparation for the founding of the Legion's Destiny chapter, set to be founded within the city of Qeynos in Everquest 2, where I shall remain as Guildmaster.<BR><BR>We wish our comrades in the old Norrath well, and know that they will do fine without our nightly contributions.  Both chapters will continue to follow the same standards of conduct that we've maintained during our six years of service.<BR><BR>Any who desire to join the Legacy chapter of the Legion are advised to contact Lady Gentlewind directly, or to visit their Guildhall at www.legion-whiterose.com .<BR><BR>
							<br><BR>
							 - Kendricke<BR><BR>
							</p>
							<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?add=y&Index=582">[Add Comment]</a>&nbsp;
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=582">[View Comments]</a>



					<BR><BR></TD></TR>

				</td>			
			</tr></table>
